<sect2 xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" id="gimp-filter-long-shadow">
  <title>Sombra projetada</title>

  <indexterm>
    <primary>Filtros</primary>
    <secondary>Sombra projetada</secondary>
  </indexterm>
  <indexterm>
    <primary>Sombra projetada</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <sect3>
    <title>Visão geral</title>
    <para>
      This GEGL-based filter
      simplifies creating long shadows in several visual styles.
    </para>
    <note>
      <para>
        It is available if the selected layer holds an Alpha channel
        (see <xref linkend="gimp-layer-alpha-add"/>).
        Otherwise, it is disabled.
      </para>
    </note>
  </sect3>

  <sect3>
    <title>Ativando o filtro</title>
    <para>
      This filter is found in the main menu under
      <menuchoice>
        <guimenu>Filters</guimenu>
        <guisubmenu>Light and Shadow</guisubmenu>
        <guimenuitem>Long Shadow…</guimenuitem>
      </menuchoice>.
    </para>
  </sect3>

  <sect3>
    <title>Opções</title>
    <figure>
      <title>Opções do filtro <quote>Sombra projetada</quote></title>
      <mediaobject>
        <imageobject>
    <imagedata fileref="images/filters/light-and-shadow/long-shadow-dialog.png" format="PNG"/>
        </imageobject>
      </mediaobject>
    </figure>
    <variablelist>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Predefinições</term>
        <term><quote>Tipo de entrada</quote></term>
        <term>Recorte</term>
        <term>Opções de mesclagem</term>
        <term>Pré-visualização</term>
        <term>Mesclar filtro</term>
        <term>Visualização dividida</term>
        <listitem>
          <xi:include href="../about-common-features.xml"/>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Estilo</term>
        <listitem>
          <mediaobject>
            <imageobject>
              <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/examples/light-and-shadow/long-shadow-ex-orig-example.png"/>
            </imageobject>
            <caption>
              Original image.
            </caption>
          </mediaobject>
          <mediaobject>
            <imageobject>
              <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/examples/light-and-shadow/long-shadow-ex-orig-dialog.png"/>
            </imageobject>
            <caption>
              The layers of the image. The text layer was created via
              the "Layers to Image Size" function in the "Layer" menu.
            </caption>
          </mediaobject>
          <para>
            <guilabel>Finite</guilabel> is the default style. Other available
            styles are <guilabel>Infinite</guilabel>,
            <guilabel>Fading</guilabel>,
            and <guilabel>Fading (fixed length)</guilabel>.
          </para>
          <figure>
            <title>Exemplo de <quote>ângulo</quote></title>
            <mediaobject>
              <imageobject>
                <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/examples/light-and-shadow/long-shadow-ex-default.png"/>
              </imageobject>
              <caption>Ângulo de 45° (padrão)</caption>
            </mediaobject>
            <mediaobject>
              <imageobject>
                <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/examples/light-and-shadow/long-shadow-ex-infinite.png"/>
              </imageobject>
              <caption>Infinito</caption>
            </mediaobject>
            <mediaobject>
              <imageobject>
                <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/examples/light-and-shadow/long-shadow-ex-fading.png"/>
              </imageobject>
              <caption>Avançando</caption>
            </mediaobject>
            <mediaobject>
              <imageobject>
                <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/examples/light-and-shadow/long-shadow-ex-fixlength.png"/>
              </imageobject>
              <caption>Avançando (comprimento fixo); comprimento = 30</caption>
            </mediaobject>
          </figure>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Ângulo</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>Ângulo da sombra, em graus.</para>
          <mediaobject>
            <imageobject>
              <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/examples/light-and-shadow/long-shadow-ex-angle.png"/>
            </imageobject>
            <caption>Ângulo de 15°</caption>
          </mediaobject>
          </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Comprimento = 1,5</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Shadow length, in pixels. Only available when
            <guilabel>Style</guilabel> is set to
            <guilabel>Finite</guilabel> or
            <guilabel>Fading (fixed length)</guilabel>.
           </para>
          <mediaobject>
            <imageobject>
              <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/examples/light-and-shadow/long-shadow-ex-length.png"/>
            </imageobject>
            <caption>Comprimento = 1,5</caption>
          </mediaobject>
         </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Midpoint</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            Shadow fade midpoint. Only available when
            <guilabel>Style</guilabel> is set to
            <guilabel>Fading</guilabel> or
            <guilabel>Fading (fixed length)</guilabel>.
           </para>
         </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Cor</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            You can choose the color of the shadow here. Just click on the
            color swatch, and select a color when the color selector pops up,
            or use the eye-dropper to pick a color from the image.
          </para>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
      <varlistentry>
        <term>Mostrar posição</term>
        <listitem>
          <para>
            The <quote>Output composition</quote> selects how the output of
            this filter will be determined. There are three choices:
          </para>
          <itemizedlist>
            <listitem>
              <para>
                <guilabel>Shadow plus image</guilabel> will output both the
                input image and the created shadow. This is the default.
              </para>
            </listitem>
            <listitem>
              <para>
                <guilabel>Shadow only</guilabel> will output only the created
                shadow.
              </para>
            </listitem>
            <listitem>
              <para>
                <guilabel>Shadow minus image</guilabel> will output the
                created shadow but subtracts the area hidden by the image.
              </para>
            </listitem>
          </itemizedlist>
          <figure>
            <title>Exemplo de <quote>Permitir redimensionamento</quote></title>
            <mediaobject>
              <imageobject>
                <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/examples/light-and-shadow/long-shadow-ex-shadonly.png"/>
              </imageobject>
              <caption>
                <para>Sombra apenas</para>
              </caption>
            </mediaobject>
            <mediaobject>
              <imageobject>
                <imagedata format="PNG" fileref="images/filters/examples/light-and-shadow/long-shadow-ex-shadminus.png"/>
              </imageobject>
              <caption>
                <para>Sombra menos imagem</para>
              </caption>
            </mediaobject>
          </figure>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
  </sect3>
</sect2>
